# Normalize the working tree to LF on every platform.
#
# Windows checkouts default to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites files to CRLF
# on checkout. That breaks two things LunarForge depends on:
#
#   1. gofmt treats a CRLF-terminated .go file as unformatted, so the `gofmt -l`
#      step in scripts/verify.sh flags every file in the repo.
#   2. A verify script checked out with CRLF fails on POSIX shells with a
#      confusing "bad interpreter" error.
#
# Declaring the endings here overrides autocrlf, so the tree is identical
# everywhere and the same ritual passes on Linux, macOS, and Windows.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Spelled out for the two that actually break, so the intent survives edits.
*.go  text eol=lf
*.sh  text eol=lf

# PowerShell 7 (what CI and modern Windows use) reads LF fine, so these stay
# normalized with everything else rather than carving out a CRLF exception.
*.ps1 text eol=lf
